[3b] Regression diagnostics (linearity, homoscedasticity, normality)...
  --- Regression diagnostics (autosomal training genes, Human LCL (ribonn)) ---
  Normality of TE (actual, log2 scale, n=9,776): skew = 0.453, excess kurtosis = 0.480, D'Agostino K^2 p = 1.1e-80, Jarque-Bera p = 8.54e-94
  Normality of residuals: skew = 0.291, excess kurtosis = 0.760, D'Agostino K^2 p = 2.13e-57, Jarque-Bera p = 8.42e-82
  Homoscedasticity (Breusch-Pagan): LM stat = 202.677, p = 4.2e-17
  Linearity (Ramsey RESET, power=3 on fitted values): F = 88.651, p = 7.02e-39
  (in each test, p < 0.05 => reject the null of normality / homoscedasticity / linearity)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/ribonn/LCL/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_te_histogram_ribonn_LCL.png
